set j+916, P0.\n- `main` in dhcp6s (md5 23e37960) fmt/cmdexec P0.\n- dnsproxy ff_udp_set_remote_url / udp_open / ff_rtsp_connect (md5 01312699) — wait, that md5 is probably dnsproxy? Actually ff_ functions (ffmpeg) suggest it's a UPnP/ffmpeg-enabled media daemon... hmm, 01312699 could be minidlnad? Let me check which binary 01312699 is. minidlnad from identification IN-008 has libavformat — yes! minidlnad links libavformat.so.54, libavutil.so.51, libexif, libid3tag, libFLAC, libvorbis, libtiff — ffmpeg-based. So 0x7590c etc. are in minidlnad. minidlnad listens on TCP (probably 8200 for media). Its ff_ functions might be part of the minidlna's internal \"ffmpeg thumbnail\" pipeline, not directly network reachable.\n\nPriorities: the highest-value targets for public PoC:\n1. httpd — port 80, with many handlers. Command injection in form handlers is common.\n2. ipcserver — custom TP-Link daemon, likely involves raw commands.\n3. dnsproxy","stream":true,"block":0}

