data: {"seq":231,"ts":"2026-08-22T15:28:16.454Z","text":"dhcp6s 控制通道 handler 是 sub_404BE0。查看它如何解析控制命令并调用 system ","stream":true,"block":1}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":232,"ts":"2026-08-22T15:28:16.837Z","text":"This is dhcp6s main — the standard DHCPv6 server. `sub_40F0F8` (vsprintf+system) is called... The call trace found no callers (probably because the callers call it via the control channel dispatcher function pointer `sub_404BE0`). In dhcp6s, the control channel commands (via dhcp6_ctl_acceptcommand with handler sub_404BE0) might call the log/exec function. Wait actually the standard dhcp6s has a function `dhcp6_ctl_log` or \"client6_send\"... The system() in dhcp6s — hmm.\n\nActually, this is the KAME dhcp6s with TP-Link modifications. The control channel (`-k ctlkey`/`-p ctlport`) accepts commands on a TCP port. If that port is public (IN-003 says dhcp6c binds tcp public), an attacker could connect and issue commands. Let me look at sub_404BE0 (the control command handler for dhcp6s).","stream":true,"block":0}

