 was empty; but the attack surface AI review said \"get_duid chain to sub_40F0F8 where vsprintf(s,format,arg) then system(s), format possibly argv/network controlled\". get_duid is in main. Let me look at get_duid and other callers of sub_40F0F8 (maybe dataflow via function pointer). Actually in dhcp6s KAME upstream, there is no system() call... TP-Link added it? Let me grep the dhcp6s binary for strings like \"sh -c\" or use the call graph on the module level. Try call_trace in direction=in on \"fwgraph_3a1f3c822c22.dhcp6s_23e37960.0x40f0f8_sub_40F0F8.sub_40F0F8\".","stream":false,"block":0}

