data: {"seq":701,"ts":"2026-08-22T15:33:01.896Z","text":"uclited uses swChkPasswordCfg (0x4d4f58) for auth. Let me look at uclited more seriously now — it's the TP-Link \"user config\" daemon and has an authentication check with a config password. In many TP-Link firmwares, the uclited daemon serves a management protocol on TCP port 20005, and the auth is only a fixed/weak check or can be bypassed (e.g., \"password\" from nvram \"sysPasswd\" default \"admin\"), and it historically","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":702,"ts":"2026-08-22T15:33:02.256Z","text":"uclited uses swChkPasswordCfg (0x4d4f58) for auth. Let me look at uclited more seriously now — it's the TP-Link \"user config\" daemon and has an authentication check with a config password. In many TP-Link firmwares, the uclited daemon serves a management protocol on TCP port 20005, and the auth is only a fixed/weak check or can be bypassed (e.g., \"password\" from nvram \"sysPasswd\" default \"admin\"), and it historically has **command injection via the smart-config XML: `command` elements executed with system()**. The FormatCmd functions (","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":703,"ts":"2026-08-22T15:33:02.637Z","text":"uclited uses swChkPasswordCfg (0x4d4f58) for auth. Let me look at uclited more seriously now — it's the TP-Link \"user config\" daemon and has an authentication check with a config password. In many TP-Link firmwares, the uclited daemon serves a management protocol on TCP port 20005, and the auth is only a fixed/weak check or can be bypassed (e.g., \"password\" from nvram \"sysPasswd\" default \"admin\"), and it historically has **command injection via the smart-config XML: `command` elements executed with system()**. The FormatCmd functions (pppoeFormatCmd etc.) plus swChkPasswordCfg suggests uclited takes XML config → builds shell commands. This is exactly the kind of chain I want.\n\nLet me look at uclited's network entry","stream":true,"block":0}

