data: {"seq":711,"ts":"2026-08-22T15:33:04.804Z","text":"uclited uses swChkPasswordCfg (0x4d4f58) for auth. Let me look at uclited more seriously now — it's the TP-Link \"user config\" daemon and has an authentication check with a config password. In many TP-Link firmwares, the uclited daemon serves a management protocol on TCP port 20005, and the auth is only a fixed/weak check or can be bypassed (e.g., \"password\" from nvram \"sysPasswd\" default \"admin\"), and it historically has **command injection via the smart-config XML: `command` elements executed with system()**. The FormatCmd functions (pppoeFormatCmd etc.) plus swChkPasswordCfg suggests uclited takes XML config → builds shell commands. This is exactly the kind of chain I want.\n\nLet me look at uclited's network entry: StartMiniServer, and where requests get dispatched (the XML parser + command handler). Find functions like \"UcProcess\" or \"wcProcess\" or \"request_handle\". Search uclited for \"proc\" functions.","stream":false,"block":0}

