data: {"seq":794,"ts":"2026-08-22T15:33:48.856Z","text":"sub_46A054 is the SSDP/UPnP notification loop: accepts TCP (sub_46A674 handles connection) and reads UDP SSDP. The UDP v14 socket reads 25 bytes (`0x19`) — small. TCP connections go to sub_46A674 — HTTP processing (the mini HTTP server). Since sub_46A674 receives HTTP requests on a TCP socket, it could trigger the XML/command processing. Let me look at sub_46A674 and the HTTP request handling chain. This is TP-Link's \"MiniServer\" (UPnP device description server). But does HTTP handling reach Execute* functions? These Execute* are usually triggered by httpd via uclited's config callback mechanism — they run when uclited receives configuration from its message framework, not directly from HTTP.\n\nActually the uclited architecture: uclited exposes a **message server** (ucm_msgTaskCreate / mq) where httpd pushes config changes. The network-facing TCP might be just for the Tether app (port 20005 XML). The AS-011 final_handler StartMiniServer suggests the TCP listener is the mini HTTP server.\n\nLet me look at sub_46A674 (per-connection handler) — that's where HTTP parsing happens; check if it parses XML POST (with attacker content) and dispatches \"command\".","stream":true,"block":0}

