on (inherited from overflow) become the \"icon\" path arg → might be used in realpath/strcpy into a file path → could lead to arbitrary file access. Interesting but messy.\n\nGiven v12 is used as URL query parsing buffer in SendResp_dlnafile/SendResp_thumbnail (they parse \"?albumID=xxx&objectID=...\" style), and SendResp_thumbnail(a1, v12) will treat v12 as the URL \"%6dx%6d\" (thumbnail request format) — attacker URL bytes flow into sscanf(\"%6dx%6d\") and file path construction → potential file read/DoS but not code exec.\n\nThis is still a legit unauthenticated memory-corruption finding (CWE-121) on a public service. Without canary (verify checksec?), impact = DoS/corruption. It's worth reporting with static-only confidence (≤0.6). But the write is bounded (511 bytes) and doesn't hit saved regs — so \"verified\" claim would","stream":true,"block":0}

